{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>\"And he shall lay his hand\" is written regarding cattle</b> — and regarding sheep it is written \"his hand,\" and regarding goats \"his hand.\" For cattle are strong and can bear the leaning, for one must lean upon it with all his strength — unlike sheep and goats. Therefore \"את\" is written, implying with slackness. Regarding cattle it is written \"whether a male or a female\"; regarding sheep \"a male or a female\" — for he required \"or\" to include the פלגס, and without it, no inclusion is implied; and regarding goats, male and female are not mentioned at all, for a goat's nature is always to bear male and female together, and presumably he will slaughter the male and leave the female for his household's livelihood. Regarding cattle it is written \"and the sons of Aharon shall burn it\" — plural; regarding sheep \"and the kohen shall burn it\" — for cattle requires many kohanim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:52.195746873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}